 - Fixed competing `task advance` calls publishing an executable exchange before journal ownership succeeded. New exchanges remain inert in `prepared` state until their exact operation intent is persisted, including crash-safe promotion on recovery.
 - Fixed competing `task advance` calls replaying the same long-running formal verification. Formal checks now hold the task execution lease, PID-backed lease ownership distinguishes a live long run from a crashed owner without relying on an 11-minute age cutoff, and an interrupted local verification receives an exact-key replacement when the task fingerprint has advanced.
 
